{"name":"Sandpit","hex":"#9e7c5e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sandpit","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place or pit from which sand is excavated.","A children’s play area consisting of a large container filled with sand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sandpit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sandpit","blocks":[{"text":"A sandpit or sandbox is a low, wide container or shallow depression filled with soft (beach) sand in which children can play. Sharp sand is not suitable for such use. Many homeowners with children build sandpits in their backyards because, unlike most playground equipment, they can be easily and cheaply constructed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Sandbox_Lawn_Jam_Our_Community_Place_Harrisonburg_VA_June_2008.jpg/330px-Sandbox_Lawn_Jam_Our_Community_Place_Harrisonburg_VA_June_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandpit","wikidata":"Q213454"},{"title":"Sandpit (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Sandpit (1989–2003) was a Brazilian Champion Thoroughbred racehorse that also met with considerable success racing in the United States. In a career that lasted from 1992 until 1997, he ran forty times and won fourteen races. Which is a winning percentage of 35%."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandpit_(horse)","wikidata":"Q7416518"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Sandpit.jpg/500px-Sandpit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Sandpit.jpg/1280px-Sandpit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Sandpit.jpg/500px-Sandpit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sandpit with toy tools used by children to play in s